    "problem": "This paper investigates how climate models simulate La Plata Basin precipitation variability, focusing on the challenge of distinguishing between the effects of remote sea surface temperature forcing and internal atmospheric variability, which creates uncertainty and simulation errors.",
    "method": "This study uses an ensemble of nine atmosphere-only GCM experiments and a coupled ocean-atmosphere model to investigate the respective roles of remote sea surface temperature forcing and internal atmospheric variability on spring precipitation in the La Plata Basin.",
    "task": "The task is to investigate the role of remote sea surface temperature forcing in modulating spring precipitation variability in the La Plata Basin using an ensemble of General Circulation Model (GCM) experiments and comparing them with a coupled ocean-atmosphere model.",
